KNOWNBUG
while1.sv
--bound 2
^\[main\.p0\] always \(##1 main\.x == 3\): PROVED up to bound 2$
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
A while statement with an elaboration-time-constant loop condition inside an
always block (IEEE 1800-2017 12.7.4). The type checker accepts it
(verilog_typecheckt::convert_while), but verilog_rtl_buildert::build_statement
in src/verilog/verilog_rtl.cpp has no case for ID_while and aborts with
"statement `while' is not supported by RTL construction" (CONVERSION ERROR).
A constant-bounded while loop should be unrolled during RTL construction the
same way build_for unrolls for loops; the former verilog_synthesis module did
this in synth_while (removed in commit a445c7fd). The loop body runs exactly
three times, so x must equal 3.
